{"id": "EUVD-2026-97646", "enisaUuid": "0173c4b1-4526-3b11-8714-64e27df09370", "description": "DOMPurify from 3.4.13 before 3.4.16 contains a cross-site scripting vulnerability because IN_PLACE mode fails to neutralize subtrees detached by afterSanitizeElements or afterSanitizeAttributes hooks. Attackers can supply markup with on* handlers inside a wrapper removed by such hooks, leaving handlers armed on the live DOM to execute script in the victim origin.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:53:48", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify/security/advisories/GHSA-p98j-92pf-mc4p", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dompurify-from-3.4.13-before-3.4.16-dom-xss-via-in-place-aftersanitize-hooks"], "aliases": ["GHSA-59fh-8xxf-p69h", "CVE-2026-109344"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3992417b-1324-346e-b113-36a10abfcef2", "product": {"name": "DOMPurify", "vendor": {"name": "cure53"}}, "product_version": "3.4.13 <3.4.16"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6ffcb6ee-a14c-3a4f-a980-929f3c5678c0", "vendor": {"name": "cure53"}}], "isExploited": false}